---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { EMAIL, GITHUB_URL, LINKEDIN_URL } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Zach Ross: software engineer building MCP infrastructure for AI assistants, previously five years on Amazon Music's royalties and FinTech teams."
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I'm a software engineer at Haselwood Group, where I design and build our
      Model Context Protocol (MCP) architecture in Python with fastmcp. It
      serves self-hosted AI assistants running on Ollama. Connecting a model to
      data is the easy part. The harder engineering problem is deciding what the
      model should never see, so I design connector boundaries over our data
      pipelines and APIs that let internal workflows be automated while
      sensitive customer and financial data stays out of reach. We're a small
      team, so I also own our web applications, APIs, data pipelines, and
      infrastructure end to end.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before that, I spent five years at Amazon Music on the Music Royalties and
      FinTech teams, where I was promoted from SDE I to SDE II. I built Apache
      Spark pipelines on AWS EMR that calculated royalties and fed accounting
      and vendor reporting, along with the APIs, ledger, and disbursement
      systems that paid labels and publishers.
    </p>
    <p>
      My path into engineering wasn't the typical one. I studied German and
      History, worked as a German-language catalog specialist for Prime Video,
      and moved into software through Amazon's Technical Academy. That route
      taught me to learn quickly and to stay close to the people who actually
      use what I build, whether that's accountants, music partners, or the
      business users relying on our assistants today.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      The best way to reach me is email: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
      . You can also find me on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a> and{" "}
      <a href={LINKEDIN_URL}>LinkedIn</a>, or download my{" "}
      <a href="/resume.pdf">resume (PDF)</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
